      "content": "BNB leads for half a day with +3.596%; BTC steps onto 77,032—who’s buying while the bulls are ready to eat at midday?\n\nMidday report first—let’s look at what stands out.\n\nBNB is up +3.596% in half a day: it was pushed from the intraday low of 721.24 all the way to 754.71. Its foot is firmly planted on the daily sell level at 745.58. While some projects are still doing the “compare misery” and drawing up promises, they’ve already cast a vote with real money. Current price 752.2—so strong it doesn’t even need friends.\n\nBTC is getting big things done without saying a word: current price 77,526.1. It’s back above the daily sell level of 77,032.13, and it’s only a few dozen dollars away from the intraday high of 77,572.4. The key is the funding rate—funding rate is 0.008629%. Even though it’s up 1.277%, it’s still sitting on the floor. That suggests this move isn’t just “artificially fat” from leverage piling in. If the market were truly overheated, the funding rate would have flown.\n\nOver 24 hours, trading volume is 9.57B USDT—volume and attitude match.\n\nETH has that annoying “precision tool” vibe. Current price 2,481.04: up 1.557%, but it still refuses to take the first step, stuck right at the doorway of the daily sell level 2,482.7, missing just a little push. Break above it and the upside opens up; if it can’t, a pullback to 2,411.25 will line up again. Funding rate is 0.009624%. The bulls aren’t getting carried away either—actually a good sign.\n\nXRP +1.923%. It’s holding above 1.31, with the baseline at 1.28. No extra talk.\n\nTime for some toxic honesty: the most expensive thing right now isn’t coins—it’s the act of chasing after the price. BTC moved from 75,975 to 77,526.1, and some people are already lined up at the gate of 77,572.4 taking photos—those who were on the top blowing in the wind still haven’t come down yet.\n\nHere’s the direction I give: bulls are in control. BNB is leading; funding is steady—not wild; all four major coins are above their daily sell levels. That’s data, not faith. But “bulls in control” doesn’t mean “chasing is in control.” A pullback that holds above 77,032.13 keeps the structure intact. If it breaks below 76,503.57, put away the dreams first. 75,857.33 is the bottom line—if that breaks, don’t argue with reality.\n\nGive levels, not impulsiveness. After lunch, watch 2,482.7 closely: whether ETH breaks this line will decide the script for the afternoon. Meeting adjourned—time to eat.\n\n$BTC  daily sell level: $77032 daily buy level: $75857\n$ETH  daily sell level: $2482.7 daily buy level: $2411.25\n$BNB  daily sell level: $745.58 daily buy level: $726.72\n$BTC #BTC $ETH #ETH",
